# ITSM agentic — environment configuration.
# cp .env.example .env && replace the placeholder values. .env is gitignored.
#
# ── Where to get the weftd / tenant credentials ──
# Register at the official Weft console: https://weft-kit.dev
# Once your tenant is provisioned, the console shows:
#   • WEFTD_BASE     — the weftd control-plane URL (shown on the API Keys page)
#   • WEFT_API_KEY   — a tenant API key (mint it under API Keys)
#   • WEFT_TENANT_ID — your tenant ID
#
# The weftd/LLM creds below are required for skill provisioning (the agent layer
# built by the integrate-weft-kit skill on top of the classic ITSM backend).

# The OPENAI_* vars configure the remote weftd control plane's LLM endpoint.
# The local ITSM server only reads OPENAI_MODEL (written into the skill
# definition at provision time); the rest seed weftd's LLM configuration.
# All vars are kept here so the file can serve as a single config source for
# both the local app and your weftd deployment.

# ── OpenAI-compatible LLM endpoint (remote weftd) ──
# OPENAI_BASE_URL points at the OpenAI-compatible /v1 endpoint weftd should use.
# OPENAI_MODELS is the comma-separated model catalog weftd should register.
# OPENAI_MODEL is the default model used when a run omits `model` (also written
# into the skill definition by the local provisioner).
OPENAI_API_KEY=replace_with_openai_compatible_api_key
OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://your-openai-compatible-endpoint.example.com/v1
OPENAI_MODELS=your-model-name
OPENAI_MODEL=your-model-name

# ── Remote weftd (the control plane) ──
# WEFTD_BASE: shown on the API Keys page of the Weft console (https://weft-kit.dev).
#   Replace the placeholder below with the value from the console.
# WEFT_API_KEY: tenant API key from the Weft console (https://weft-kit.dev).
# WEFT_TENANT_ID: tenant ID that owns the API key.
WEFTD_BASE=https://your-weftd-endpoint.example.com
WEFT_API_KEY=replace_with_tenant_api_key
WEFT_TENANT_ID=replace_with_tenant_id

# ── ITSM server (optional) ──
# ITSM_PORT defaults to 19755 if omitted.
ITSM_PORT=19755

# ── CORS (production: REQUIRED, dev: optional) ──
# Comma-separated exact origins. Unset = dev-only permissive `*` WITHOUT
# credentials (the Vite dev proxy makes it same-origin; safe for non-credentialed
# reads, inert for credentialed, so the session cookie is never exposed
# cross-origin). For any non-localhost deployment, set this to enable credentialed
# cross-origin. NEVER set `["*"]` + credentials together — Starlette reflects
# ANY origin WITH credentials (the textbook misconfig).
# ITSM_CORS_ORIGINS=https://itsm.example.com,https://www.example.com
# ITSM_CORS_ORIGINS=
